     ADK Sessions vs FastAPI - Key Differences

  ADK Sessions (What We Built)

  - Purpose: Intelligent conversation state management following Google ADK best practices
  - Core Features:
    - ✅ Persistent conversation memory across interactions
    - ✅ Topic detection and context awareness
    - ✅ Agent routing and delegation tracking
    - ✅ Performance metrics and analytics
    - ✅ Contextual suggestions based on conversation flow
    - ✅ Session lifecycle management (create, persist, restore, close)

  FastAPI (What It Provides)

  - Purpose: HTTP API framework for web requests/responses
  - Core Features:
    - ✅ REST endpoints (/api/v1/sessions/create, /api/v1/agent/chat)
    - ✅ Request validation with Pydantic models
    - ✅ WebSocket support for real-time communication
    - ✅ CORS handling for frontend integration
    - ✅ API documentation (automatic OpenAPI/Swagger)

